This is the plan for the series agreed in "[RFC] commit style" [1]:
four commit messages in the order they would land, with no docs,
tests, or code yet. It is text for review, not for applying. To
change a message, reply with your version quoted under mine, and I
will fold it into my commits.

The series is based on trunk.

Changes in v2:
- Plain text in one mail instead of format-patch output, as agreed
  in the thread.
- Dropped the two libexec/mail commits, "Collect the files
  format-patch.sh writes" and "Check commit messages before
